-- A function a platform keeps in a JavaScript array and takes out again by
-- a method whose name is made at run time, `frames[name]()`, is still a
-- function the program calls (#685): `--check-call-graph`, which the
-- corpus's release pass builds with, would make the call throw if fact 3's
-- call graph missed it. Expected `42`.
import Node exposing (Program)
import Probe


main : Program
main = Node.printLines [ String.fromInt (Probe.viaComputed (λx → x + 1) 41) ]
